392-## 2. Product and operator model
393-
394-### 2.1 Terms
395-
396-| Term | Normative definition |
397-| --- | --- |
398-| Logical session | The provider-independent durable unit identified by <code>session_id</code>. A resume does not create a new logical session. |
399-| Session name | A mesh-unique human alias of 1–64 characters matching <code>[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}</code>. |
400:| Owner | The one host selected by the winning lease that MAY run or resume the logical session. |
401-| Replica | A host holding synchronized durable state that MUST NOT run or resume the logical session without takeover or fork. |
402-| Host | A machine with a stable UUIDv7 <code>host_id</code>, one configured platform, and one allowlist entry. |
403-| Lease | An immutable ownership grant containing an epoch, predecessor, holder, and fencing token. |
404-| Lease epoch | A monotonically increasing positive <code>uint53</code> counter scoped to one logical session. |
405:| Fencing token | The winning <code>lease_id</code> and epoch pair carried by every owner-authored event and mutation. |
406-| Checkpoint | An immutable, validated reference set for provider, workspace, board, and session records at a safe boundary. |
407-| Fork | A new logical session and new workspace identity derived from a checkpoint, with independent lease and event history. |
408-| Workspace | One Git worktree/repository or one managed non-Git directory with a logical ID independent of its absolute path. |
409-| Workspace group | The atomic migration set for sessions sharing one checkout or otherwise requiring coordinated materialization. |
410-| Provider identity | Provider ID, native durable handle, logical workspace mapping, and non-secret backend-realm fingerprint needed to resolve a native session. |
411-| Direct session | A session launched and persisted through a provider adapter and native provider store. |
412-| Task-board session | A session whose private provider mechanics remain owned by <code>tb-sessiond</code> and cross the boundary only as an opaque official bundle. |
413-| Safe boundary | A provider-reported or adapter-proven point at which no foreground, child, scheduled, or background work can still mutate durable state. |
--
420-| Display title | Human-facing title resolved from immutable annotations and native candidates; it is not Session Record <code>name</code> or selector identity. |
421-| Continuation Plan | Immutable, content-addressed, expiring, non-mutating selection of one continuation route and all facts that execution must revalidate. |
422-| Directory Node | Separately negotiated source-local companion façade for discovery, bounded preview, enrichment, runtime observation, and directory health, backed by the same environment implementation as Provider 2 and Session Adapter 1. |
423-
424-### 2.2 Global invariants
425-
426-The following invariants are unconditional:
427-
428:1. Every non-tombstoned logical session MUST have exactly one winning lease and
429-   therefore exactly one logical owner, plus zero or more replicas.
430-2. A replica MUST NOT launch, resume, accept input for, or publish authoritative
431-   events for a logical session.
432:3. Every owner-authored event MUST carry the winning lease epoch and lease ID.
433-   A peer MUST reject lower-epoch or losing same-epoch events from the
434-   authoritative history and preserve them in a divergent-history branch.
435-4. Absolute source paths, process IDs, terminal IDs, socket names, and provider
436-   route facts MUST NOT be cross-host identity.
437-5. Provider credentials, environment secrets, authentication state, live PIDs,
438-   sockets, transient locks, and live database WAL/SHM files MUST NOT be
439-   replicated.
440-6. The live SQLite index MUST NOT be copied or synchronized. It is rebuildable
--
447-9. A deletion MUST be represented by a scoped tombstone. A receiver MUST NOT
448-   treat any tombstone as authority for a broad recursive delete.
449-10. The persisted execution profile MUST be used on both initial launch and
450-    every resume. An adapter MUST NOT silently downgrade <code>yolo</code>.
451-11. A capability not proven for the exact provider/version/platform tuple MUST
452-    be conditional, unsupported, or unknown and MUST be disabled.
453-12. A task-board session MUST use the official opaque bridge. <code>ax</code>
454-    MUST NOT read or mutate private <code>tb-sessiond</code> state.
455:13. <code>ax sync --all</code> MUST NOT change ownership or launch a runtime. It
456-    converges only immutable objects and policy-allowed derived projections.
457-14. Automatic continuation is permitted only for one uniquely safe,
458:    non-mutating route. Takeover, fork, move, and every ambiguous route MUST
459-    remain a pure plan until explicit confirmation; a non-interactive caller
460-    that has not selected the action receives
461-    <code>interactive_choice_required</code>.
462-15. Destination broker and provider-auth readiness MUST be proved before any
463-    takeover ownership commit. Remote attach always targets the current owner
464-    and creates no runtime. Graceful takeover creates a destination runtime only
465-    after verified source stop and ownership commit. Force takeover is the
466-    explicit recovery exception when source stop cannot be proved: its winning
