+## 2026-09-22
+
+### BUG-260917-3lddu0 — superseded leases are refused before append admission
+
+- FIX: `Repository.AppendEvent` now calls `checkWinningLease` after loading the durable lease winner and before `checkAppend`. Lower-epoch events refuse `ErrStaleLease`; same-epoch losing leases refuse `ErrDivergentBranch`. Refused branch bytes remain immutable and addressable, while the authoritative chain is unchanged. Historical replay intentionally does not apply this owner-side gate.
+- REPRO: the exact trunk baseline at `799c338e401fca0b24859c0b870cd665927209f2` was driven through an adapted production `AppendEvent` probe: a successor won while the tail still named A, then A's append returned `err=<nil>` and the negative expected stale refusal. The archived review probe 15 records the old blast radius verbatim: losing-lease `profile.changed` drove `profile=yolo` with mapping `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`. The candidate test `TestLosingLeaseProfileEventIgnored` now refuses the append and proves `Run` cannot use that source.
+- AC: 2 of 2 leaf rows are driven. The gate × production-entry census is 8 of 8 cells: 4 lower-epoch (`AppendEvent`, `SetProfile`, `Emit`, `EmitParked`) and 4 same-epoch loser cells, with no unreachable cell. `N-stale-winning-admission` and `N-same-epoch-winning-admission` retain the gate, admit one rejected class each, and are KILLED; harmless comment SURVIVED, NOT_APPLIED and compile controls are classified separately.
+- IMPORTER DIFF: complete importer mask is `./internal/axpane ./internal/crashgate ./internal/fencing ./internal/sessckpt ./internal/sessprofile ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessstate ./internal/termbind ./internal/terminstance`. Before/after: 2,018/2,025 outcome keys; 7 named new negative-test outcomes, 0 removed, 0 changed; all 9 package summaries PASS. The seven moved inputs are the four `Emit`/`EmitParked` gate-entry tests and the `SetProfile` parent plus its two arm outcomes; direct sessrepo tests are outside the importer set and are named in the matrix.
+- TRACEABILITY: candidate registry digest re-derived as `ed6f016f73e390071743b09aded229e781d95408b0b9eeb3f134fcb87bb9a893`; exact-tree tracecheck prints `contracts=64 normative_sections=36 acceptance_cases=154 fixtures=33 compatibility_contracts=55 assigned_scopes=0` and `section coverage: bindings=69 full=4 partial=9 sliver=9 unevidenced=43 unmeasured=4 unowned=7 clauses_discharged=70/574`. Section 2.4 admits; section 5.3 correctly refuses assigned-scope admission at 7/8 partial coverage.
+- P3 DISPOSITIONS: the axpane `decide.go` “lapsed grants refuse” qualifier remains untouched and is scoped to the local-owner path; `observeRemoteWinner` structural redundancy is record-only; the grant-less remote interactive-owner step-4 product question remains unresolved and undecided; evidence records the candidate tree OID before this logbook append (`276c515c90665327b991fe1cdf78ef8086cd409c`) and keeps the exact test masks beside every row count.
+- VALIDATION: all 30 commands from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` exited 0, including full test, race, coverage, fuzz, tracecheck, catalog check, Linux/Windows builds, JSON parse, board validation, and diff check. Explicit `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` also exited 0. `task-board validate` printed pre-existing `MISSING_ACTIVITY` diagnostics but exited 0. Logs are under `.temp/BUG-260917-3lddu0/validation/`.
+- HANDOFF: final tests are in `.temp/BUG-260917-3lddu0/final-tests/`; mutation evidence is in `mutants-append-03/`; importer outcomes and tracecheck logs are task-scoped; the candidate remains UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for snapshot handoff.
